{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YX5c3nT9jB5bZLykEvpzPm","type":"tool_result","content":"87:- 1104 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\n316:- `input.touchArea()` †: where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or null while none show: keep a prompt or a box clear of it (a bottom E.Dialog does by itself)\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a m\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1107:- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n1108:- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n1109:- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n1110:- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n1111:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it \n1112:- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n1113:- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n1114:- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n1115:- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n1116:- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n1117:- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n1118:- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n1119:- `talk.game`: its game\n1120:- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n1121:- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n1122:- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n1123:- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n1124:- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n1125:- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n1126:- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n1127:- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n1128:- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n1129:- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n1130:- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n1131:- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n1132:- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n1133:- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n1672:- `story.talk`: the E.Dialog it speaks through\n83:- 1047 Audio; game.audio\n514:- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\n1050:- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n1051:- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n1052:- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n1053:- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done i\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1055:- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n1056:- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s .\n1058:- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n1059:- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n1060:- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n1061:- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n1062:- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the mus\n1064:- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n1065:- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n1066:- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n1067:- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock