{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GA5RuxVsm6PMKjnmQnRTGW","type":"tool_result","content":"  }\n  const GLOW_AT = { lamp: [.5, .2, '#ffe8a0'], streetlamp: [.5, .13, '#ffe8a0'], lantern: [.5, .55, t.lt], crystal: [.5, .6, color] };\n  p = { glowAt: GLOW_AT[name] || null, frames, glow, w: W, h: H, emissive: name === 'lamp' || name === 'crystal' || name === 'window' || name === 'lantern' || name === 'streetlamp', light: flames.length ? (name === 'crystal' ? color : name === 'lantern' ? t.lt : name === 'streetlamp' ? '#ffe0a0' : n\n  _props.set(key, p);\n  return p;\n}\nE.prop = prop;\n/** the names of the built-in props for r.prop(name, x, y, z, opts) and E.prop(name, opts) */\nE.PROPS = Object.keys(PROP_DEFAULTS);\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * 21e. SHAPES  still 3D objects written as data: named parts, each a primitive with a material, drawn from any view and\n *    facing at game size (a depth buffer per shape, shaded with the material's five tones and pattern, creases where parts\n *    meet, lit top edges, the actors' outline), with a contact shadow. docs/ASSETS.md is the card: the parts, the\n *    materials, the library, how to make one and check it headless.\n *      r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })                          // feet on (x, y, z), front toward facing\n *      E.SHAPES.stool = { about: 'a three-legged stool', mats: { w: 'oak' },\n *        parts: [['cyl','w',[0,0,8],5,1.5], ['ring',3,3,['box','w',[0,0,0],[1.5,1.5,8]]]] };\n *      map.solid('table', x, y, 0, { facing })                         // collision: bodies stop at it, land on it\n *    Units: 16 = 1 m = one tile; x east, y south, z up. A shape's origin is the middle of its footprint on the ground; it\n *    is written facing south (+y). Parts ([kind, material slot, at, ...sizes, { options }]; at is the bottom middle,\n *    except a ball's and a rock's, which is their centre):\n *      ['box', m, at, [w, d, h], { rot }]     ['cyl', m, at, r, h, { r2, seg, sq }]     ['lathe', m, at, [[r, z]...], { seg }]\n *      ['ball', m, at, r, { sz }]             ['prism', m, at, [[a, b]...], h, { axis: 'z' | 'y' | 'x' }]\n *      ['wedge', m, at, [w, d, h]]            ['rock', m, at, r, { sz, seed, rough }]\n *      ['use', id, at, { rot, scale, mats, ...params }]   ['mirror', 'x' | 'y' | 'xy', part]   ['ring', n, radius, part]\n *      ['row', n, [dx, dy, dz], part]          ['group', at, rot, [parts]]\n *    rot: a yaw in degrees, or [x, y, z] degrees. Nothing below the floor is drawn (a half-sunk rock).\n * ============================================================================= */\n/** the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the\n *  core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and your own: E.SHAPES.stool = {...}) */\n408:- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, above its feet: the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall); xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors } picks the colors, and with actors: true other bodies drawn in front hid\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game\n767:- `map.solid(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: make a shape solid in this map: map.solid(id | entry, x, y, z, o) with r.shape's placement (facing, scale, flip, params) -> the solid ({ x, y (the footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy, c, s, shape, px, py (where it was placed) }; map.solids holds them; what stands on one sorts after it). A body overlapping its span in height is pushed out of its footprint; one coming down onto it lands on its top; one wholly below passes under. Register solids before \n768:- `map.solidAt(x, y)`: solidCell at a world point\n769:- `map.solidCell(cx, cy)`: true where a cell has a wall (or is outside the map); walkable() also counts blocked floor","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b281c84-305d-4114-8ac5-d69722c0fb1c","uuid":"5336f673-904b-43e9-a1dd-00a1069e2a48","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:59:29.223Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  }\n  const GLOW_AT = { lamp: [.5, .2, '#ffe8a0'], streetlamp: [.5, .13, '#ffe8a0'], lantern: [.5, .55, t.lt], crystal: [.5, .6, color] };\n  p = { glowAt: GLOW_AT[name] || null, frames, glow, w: W, h: H, emissive: name === 'lamp' || name === 'crystal' || name === 'window' || name === 'lantern' || name === 'streetlamp', light: flames.length ? (name === 'crystal' ? color : name === 'lantern' ? t.lt : name === 'streetlamp' ? '#ffe0a0' : n\n  _props.set(key, p);\n  return p;\n}\nE.prop = prop;\n/** the names of the built-in props for r.prop(name, x, y, z, opts) and E.prop(name, opts) */\nE.PROPS = Object.keys(PROP_DEFAULTS);\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * 21e. SHAPES  still 3D objects written as data: named parts, each a primitive with a material, drawn from any view and\n *    facing at game size (a depth buffer per shape, shaded with the material's five tones and pattern, creases where parts\n *    meet, lit top edges, the actors' outline), with a contact shadow. docs/ASSETS.md is the card: the parts, the\n *    materials, the library, how to make one and check it headless.\n *      r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })                          // feet on (x, y, z), front toward facing\n *      E.SHAPES.stool = { about: 'a three-legged stool', mats: { w: 'oak' },\n *        parts: [['cyl','w',[0,0,8],5,1.5], ['ring',3,3,['box','w',[0,0,0],[1.5,1.5,8]]]] };\n *      map.solid('table', x, y, 0, { facing })                         // collision: bodies stop at it, land on it\n *    Units: 16 = 1 m = one tile; x east, y south, z up. A shape's origin is the middle of its footprint on the ground; it\n *    is written facing south (+y). Parts ([kind, material slot, at, ...sizes, { options }]; at is the bottom middle,\n *    except a ball's and a rock's, which is their centre):\n *      ['box', m, at, [w, d, h], { rot }]     ['cyl', m, at, r, h, { r2, seg, sq }]     ['lathe', m, at, [[r, z]...], { seg }]\n *      ['ball', m, at, r, { sz }]             ['prism', m, at, [[a, b]...], h, { axis: 'z' | 'y' | 'x' }]\n *      ['wedge', m, at, [w, d, h]]            ['rock', m, at, r, { sz, seed, rough }]\n *      ['use', id, at, { rot, scale, mats, ...params }]   ['mirror', 'x' | 'y' | 'xy', part]   ['ring', n, radius, part]\n *      ['row', n, [dx, dy, dz], part]          ['group', at, rot, [parts]]\n *    rot: a yaw in degrees, or [x, y, z] degrees. Nothing below the floor is drawn (a half-sunk rock).\n * ============================================================================= */\n/** the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the\n *  core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and your own: E.SHAPES.stool = {...}) */\n408:- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, above its feet: the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall); xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors } picks the colors, and with actors: true other bodies drawn in front hid\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game\n767:- `map.solid(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: make a shape solid in this map: map.solid(id | entry, x, y, z, o) with r.shape's placement (facing, scale, flip, params) -> the solid ({ x, y (the footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy, c, s, shape, px, py (where it was placed) }; map.solids holds them; what stands on one sorts after it). A body overlapping its span in height is pushed out of its footprint; one coming down onto it lands on its top; one wholly below passes under. Register solids before \n768:- `map.solidAt(x, y)`: solidCell at a world point\n769:- `map.solidCell(cx, cy)`: true where a cell has a wall (or is outside the map); walkable() also counts blocked floor","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GA5RuxVsm6PMKjnmQnRTGW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
