{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfAgpzeNVvTAHeCNyk1a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lvz6iDuJuq4KRa5PUgb9R7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"for k in \"E.rng\\|^- .rng(\" \"game.mouseGround\" \"r.marker\" \"screenDirToGround\" \"screenToGround\\|groundAt\\|toGround\" \"E.Menu\\b\" \"menu.settings\" \"game.follow\" \"game.saves\" \"r.pick\" \"tex\\.\\(checker\\|plain\\)\" \"E.Backdrop\" \"game.note\" \"FlowField\\b\" \"flow.dir\"; do echo \"== $k\"; grep -n -- \"$k\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-420 | head -4; done"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2335,"cache_read_input_tokens":108943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2335,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b281c84-305d-4114-8ac5-d69722c0fb1c","uuid":"53588273-5313-41e5-b6de-518bdcb8e0d7","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:00:52.369Z","request_id":"req_011CgfAgpdJsKj3MjepKZCbz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Lvz6iDuJuq4KRa5PUgb9R7":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-185709__x694301/work/ref && for k in \"E.rng\\|^- .rng(\" \"game.mouseGround\" \"r.marker\" \"screenDirToGround\" \"screenToGround\\|groundAt\\|toGround\" \"E.Menu\\b\" \"menu.settings\" \"game.follow\" \"game.saves\" \"r.pick\" \"tex\\.\\(checker\\|plain\\)\" \"E.Backdrop\" \"game.note\" \"FlowField\\b\" \"flow.dir\"; do echo \"== $k\"; grep -n -- \"$k\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-420 | head -4; done"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01Lvz6iDuJuq4KRa5PUgb9R7":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-185709__x694301/work/ref"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lvz6iDuJuq4KRa5PUgb9R7","type":"tool_result","content":"== E.rng\\|^- .rng(\n179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n== game.mouseGround\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n== r.marker\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n== screenDirToGround\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n== screenToGround\\|groundAt\\|toGround\n229:- `view.toGround(sx, sy)`: projected screen point -> ground point (z = 0). null in side view\n754:- `map.groundAt(x, y, r = 0, z = 1e9, step = 2)`: highest surface under a circle footprint that a body at height z can stand on (floor = 0)\n924:- `body.update(dt, map)`: move it one step: speed, friction, walls (map.collide: lower walls are walked onto), gravity and the ground under it (map.groundAt)\n== E.Menu\\b\n87:- 1104 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n== menu.settings\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n== game.follow\n480:- `game.follow(target, o = {})`: keep the camera on an object automatically (instead of calling focus every update). opts: { z: extra height to look at (default 16), lead: look ahead in the facing / moving direction }. follow(null) stops.\n== game.saves\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n== r.pick\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stan\n464:- `new E.Game({ pace })`: false draws every refresh of a fast display even when the frames can't keep up (by default it draws every other one, evenly), unless the player picks Frame rate 60\n== tex\\.\\(checker\\|plain\\)\n836:- `E.tex.checker(x, y, o = {})`: checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size }\n840:- `E.tex.plain(x, y, o = {})`: plain color with light noise, for roads, carpets and space floors. o: { base, amount }\n== E.Backdrop\n84:- 1079 Backdrops; E.Backdrop: backdrop\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, c\n1082:- `E.Backdrop.presets` †: the preset names, all ten: day, dusk, night, castle-night, city-night, desert, forest, ocean, cave, space\n== game.note\n487:- `game.note(text, seconds = 1.2)`, `game.shownNote`: a short notice at the top of the screen (zoom level, saved, ...): game.note('ZOOM 1.5x', 1). game.shownNote is the one showing, { text, end } (end in game.real seconds), or null: a game that draws it its own way takes it and sets shownNote to null\n== FlowField\\b\n20:- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n73:- 815 Flow field; E.FlowField: flow\n817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n== flow.dir\n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b281c84-305d-4114-8ac5-d69722c0fb1c","uuid":"6fb1ffc8-d786-40e5-b1ea-bbd6e2fc21ea","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:00:52.430Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"== E.rng\\|^- .rng(\n179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n== game.mouseGround\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n== r.marker\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n== screenDirToGround\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n== screenToGround\\|groundAt\\|toGround\n229:- `view.toGround(sx, sy)`: projected screen point -> ground point (z = 0). null in side view\n754:- `map.groundAt(x, y, r = 0, z = 1e9, step = 2)`: highest surface under a circle footprint that a body at height z can stand on (floor = 0)\n924:- `body.update(dt, map)`: move it one step: speed, friction, walls (map.collide: lower walls are walked onto), gravity and the ground under it (map.groundAt)\n== E.Menu\\b\n87:- 1104 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n== menu.settings\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n== game.follow\n480:- `game.follow(target, o = {})`: keep the camera on an object automatically (instead of calling focus every update). opts: { z: extra height to look at (default 16), lead: look ahead in the facing / moving direction }. follow(null) stops.\n== game.saves\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n== r.pick\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stan\n464:- `new E.Game({ pace })`: false draws every refresh of a fast display even when the frames can't keep up (by default it draws every other one, evenly), unless the player picks Frame rate 60\n== tex\\.\\(checker\\|plain\\)\n836:- `E.tex.checker(x, y, o = {})`: checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size }\n840:- `E.tex.plain(x, y, o = {})`: plain color with light noise, for roads, carpets and space floors. o: { base, amount }\n== E.Backdrop\n84:- 1079 Backdrops; E.Backdrop: backdrop\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, c\n1082:- `E.Backdrop.presets` †: the preset names, all ten: day, dusk, night, castle-night, city-night, desert, forest, ocean, cave, space\n== game.note\n487:- `game.note(text, seconds = 1.2)`, `game.shownNote`: a short notice at the top of the screen (zoom level, saved, ...): game.note('ZOOM 1.5x', 1). game.shownNote is the one showing, { text, end } (end in game.real seconds), or null: a game that draws it its own way takes it and sets shownNote to null\n== FlowField\\b\n20:- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n73:- 815 Flow field; E.FlowField: flow\n817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n== flow.dir\n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Lvz6iDuJuq4KRa5PUgb9R7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
